# Security Testing & Assurance Reviewer Rule v1.0 STRICT

**Do not inline-audit.** Invoke **`security_testing_reviewer`** -> `.cursor/agents/security_testing_reviewer.md`.

## References

| Artifact | Path |
|---|---|
| Policy | `.cursor/skills/security_testing_reviewer/POLICY.md` |
| Scan skill | `.cursor/skills/security_testing_reviewer/SKILL.md` |
| Report path | `AI/security_testing_reviewer/security_testing_reviewer_report.md` |
| Report line | `security_testing_reviewer v1.0 STRICT` |

**POLICY.md wins.**

## Invoke when

Use before deploy or when CI/CD pipeline definitions, ZAP configurations, scan scripts, or release processes change.

Skip for generated output, `target/`, `node_modules/`, and docs-only edits unless the docs define security testing policy.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **No DAST scan at all before production is always FAIL.**
2. **Unresolved High/Critical ZAP alerts shipped to production is always FAIL.**
3. **Skipping a scan tool because it is missing is MANUAL_REVIEW, never PASS.**

## Finding table

Every finding includes:

| Row | Content |
|---|---|
| Evidence | Bad line or runtime proof from project |
| Policy Rule | POLICY.md - CHECK-ID - citation |
| Pattern | SKILL.md section 8 pattern |
| Mechanism | Plain English + framework/API names |
| Security property | What must be true after fix |
| Prohibited | Short label only |
| Verify | Action + pass signal |

Allowed verdicts: **PASS**, **FAIL**, **MANUAL_REVIEW**, **N/A**. `UNCLEAR` is forbidden.
